findings.description:
The doc has no failure section. It claims adoption is "additive and reversible," but no command removes the derived architecture, retroactive entries, or managed blocks. Re-run overwrite policy covers only the concept. Unaddressed cases include:

- an agent stopping mid-step 5 (see the FAIL above);
- a graph build that fails after writing a partial comprehension doc, which cf then reads by filename;
- a prompt fetch that fails;
- two runs racing on one checkout.

The project's review rules require failure-mode enumeration for each new I/O path. The directory walk, git history, CI root checks, prompt fetch and comprehension read have none.

Fix: add a per-step failure table with the observable signal for each failure. Define the revert as removing the files a run added, identified by provenance.
